    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 205788,
    "poster_id": 652,
    "post_rendered": "Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72f6578503fd314277e24211f29524dbeb66abf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ I$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" > is incenter of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b45ab3d3ac6f84f8948eae63deadbb5ae0da447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20aba2bc8efd2194f199279168706729cae0a0e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ l&#039;$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"14\" > is a line tangent to the incircle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/4/e54bfd68a71029d50fa2beb366f31db782fb0c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ l$\"  width=\"5\" height=\"12\" > be another line such that intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/014218b7557d642abf692cabb4cb8e4a90c7b1c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ AB,AC,BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" > respectively at <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d7568433f5aaf1a531cf67ccbaa9108efbf7f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ C&#039;,B&#039;,A&#039;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" >.</span> We draw a tangent from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e9e5ca4e7b865552554e5af437b055ff2627aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ A&#039;$\"  width=\"17\" height=\"14\" > to the incircle other than <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/4/e3427a9945d3b1de6a7c0b6862f3228415ea8bca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ BC$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" >,</span> and this line intersects with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20aba2bc8efd2194f199279168706729cae0a0e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ l&#039;$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"14\" > at <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b95c13282666d7120d333b503d21e9b7b0e91c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" >.</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3bb0fb8cff1812eac075b59438c375f1291a20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ B_1,C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" > are similarly defined. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2d328c35b49c1bc3e061a85dcac59dcdb4168e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ AA_1,BB_1,CC_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" > are concurrent.",
    "post_canonical": "Suppose that $ I$ is incenter of triangle $ ABC$ and $ l'$ is a line tangent to the incircle. Let $ l$ be another line such that intersects $ AB,AC,BC$ respectively at $ C',B',A'$. We draw a tangent from $ A'$ to the incircle other than $ BC$, and this line intersects with $ l'$ at $ A_1$. $ B_1,C_1$ are similarly defined. Prove that $ AA_1,BB_1,CC_1$ are concurrent.",
    "username": "Omid Hatami",
